{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to help users modify files by generating tool calls and complete file content.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\n**IMPORTANT**: You do NOT directly edit files. You generate tool calls that the system executes.\n\n## CORRECT WORKFLOW (CRITICAL):\n\n1. **Read the file first**: Generate a read_file tool call to get the current file content\n2. **Reason about changes**: Look at the file content (from tool response) and understand what needs to change\n3. **Generate COMPLETE file content**: Create the entire new file content as text (NOT a diff or patch)\n4. **Write the complete file**: Generate a write_file tool call with the complete new file content\n\nThe system will execute your tool calls. You never touch the filesystem directly.\n\n## CRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n\n- **ALWAYS generate the COMPLETE file content** in write_file, not just the changes\n- **NEVER generate diffs, patches, or partial content** - always the full file\n- **CRITICAL: When you read a file, use EXACTLY the content from read_file tool response**\n- **CRITICAL: When replacing text, change ONLY what the user specified - preserve everything else EXACTLY**\n- **CRITICAL: Do NOT add, remove, or modify any content that the user didn't explicitly request**\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- Do NOT add lines like \"done: true\" or \"more: false\" unless they were in the original file\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- If the user says \"add the content 'X'\", add ONLY 'X' - nothing else\n- If the file is EMPTY and user says \"add content 'X'\", the file should contain ONLY 'X' (no other content)\n- Do NOT add example content like \"line1: first line\" or \"existing content\" unless it is already in the file\n- Content to add/remove is usually specified in single or double quotes: 'text' or \"text\"\n- Extract the exact content from quotes - do not modify or interpret it\n- When reading a file, use ONLY the content that is actually in the file (from read_file tool response)\n- Do NOT infer or add content that wasn't in the file you read\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was (if any exists)\n- Follow the user instructions precisely and literally\n- Generate tool calls (read_file, write_file) that the system will execute\n- You never directly access or modify files - only generate tool calls and content"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Modify the file at `document.md`.\n\nWrite the following content to the file:\nLine 1: New content\nLine 2: More content\n\nRemember: Only change what is specified. Preserve all other content exactly as it is in the file."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I will read the file to see its current content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"document.md\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "", "tool_call_id": "call_a8efc26e9300"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I have read the file. Now I will make only the requested change and generate the complete updated file content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"document.md\", \"contents\": \"Line 1: New content\\nLine 2: More content\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_e3dd77343552"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done. I have made only the requested change and preserved all other content."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to help users modify files by generating tool calls and complete file content.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\n**IMPORTANT**: You do NOT directly edit files. You generate tool calls that the system executes.\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Generate tool calls (read_file, write_file) that the system will execute\n- You never directly access or modify files - only generate tool calls and content\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create default/example content unless the user explicitly requests it\n- If the user says \"create a file X\" without specifying content, create an EMPTY file\n- Do NOT add \"test: 1\" or any default content to YAML files\n- Do NOT add default structure to JSON files\n- Only create the exact content the user describes\n- If no content is specified, use write_file with empty contents: \"\"\n- Follow the user instructions precisely"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Create a new file at `document.md` with a simple Go program that prints 'Hello, World!'"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I will create the new file with the requested content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"document.md\", \"contents\": \"package main\\n\\nimport \\\"fmt\\\"\\n\\nfunc main() {\\n\\tfmt.Println(\\\"Hello, World!\\\")\\n}\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_b2928ac45ea8"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done. The file has been created."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to help users modify files by generating tool calls and complete file content.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\n**IMPORTANT**: You do NOT directly edit files. You generate tool calls that the system executes.\n\n## CORRECT WORKFLOW (CRITICAL):\n\n1. **Read the file first**: Generate a read_file tool call to get the current file content\n2. **Reason about changes**: Look at the file content (from tool response) and understand what needs to change\n3. **Generate COMPLETE file content**: Create the entire new file content as text (NOT a diff or patch)\n4. **Write the complete file**: Generate a write_file tool call with the complete new file content\n\nThe system will execute your tool calls. You never touch the filesystem directly.\n\n## CRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n\n- **ALWAYS generate the COMPLETE file content** in write_file, not just the changes\n- **NEVER generate diffs, patches, or partial content** - always the full file\n- **CRITICAL: When you read a file, use EXACTLY the content from read_file tool response**\n- **CRITICAL: When replacing text, change ONLY what the user specified - preserve everything else EXACTLY**\n- **CRITICAL: Do NOT add, remove, or modify any content that the user didn't explicitly request**\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- Do NOT add lines like \"done: true\" or \"more: false\" unless they were in the original file\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- If the user says \"add the content 'X'\", add ONLY 'X' - nothing else\n- If the file is EMPTY and user says \"add content 'X'\", the file should contain ONLY 'X' (no other content)\n- Do NOT add example content like \"line1: first line\" or \"existing content\" unless it is already in the file\n- Content to add/remove is usually specified in single or double quotes: 'text' or \"text\"\n- Extract the exact content from quotes - do not modify or interpret it\n- When reading a file, use ONLY the content that is actually in the file (from read_file tool response)\n- Do NOT infer or add content that wasn't in the file you read\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was (if any exists)\n- Follow the user instructions precisely and literally\n- Generate tool calls (read_file, write_file) that the system will execute\n- You never directly access or modify files - only generate tool calls and content"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Modify the file at `app.py`.\n\nImport datetime and update get_date to return the current date using datetime.now()\n\nRemember: Only change what is specified. Preserve all other content exactly as it is in the file."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I will read the file to see its current content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"app.py\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "def get_date():\n    return \"2024-01-01\"\n", "tool_call_id": "call_8833675622c5"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I have read the file. Now I will make only the requested change and generate the complete updated file content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"app.py\", \"contents\": \"from datetime import datetime\\n\\ndef get_date():\\n    return datetime.now().strftime(\\\"%Y-%m-%d\\\")\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_9952a96a165b"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done. I have made only the requested change and preserved all other content."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to help users modify files by generating tool calls and complete file content.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nGuidelines:\n- Do not infer missing logic\n- Do not create domain-specific content\n- Only manipulate the text the user describes\n- Follow the user instructions precisely\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files\n- If the user asks to confirm or check contents without changes, only read the file"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Check the contents of `test.txt` and confirm what is in it. Do not make any changes."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I will read the file to check its contents.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"test.txt\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "Line 1: First line\nLine 2: Second line\nLine 3: Third line", "tool_call_id": "call_acf6eb004aaa"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "The file `test.txt` contains:\n\nLine 1: First line\nLine 2: Second line\nLine 3: Third line\n\nNo changes were made as requested."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to help users modify files by generating tool calls and complete file content.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\n**IMPORTANT**: You do NOT directly edit files. You generate tool calls that the system executes.\n\n## CORRECT WORKFLOW (CRITICAL):\n\n1. **Read the file first**: Generate a read_file tool call to get the current file content\n2. **Reason about changes**: Look at the file content (from tool response) and understand what needs to change\n3. **Generate COMPLETE file content**: Create the entire new file content as text (NOT a diff or patch)\n4. **Write the complete file**: Generate a write_file tool call with the complete new file content\n\nThe system will execute your tool calls. You never touch the filesystem directly.\n\n## CRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n\n- **ALWAYS generate the COMPLETE file content** in write_file, not just the changes\n- **NEVER generate diffs, patches, or partial content** - always the full file\n- **CRITICAL: When you read a file, use EXACTLY the content from read_file tool response**\n- **CRITICAL: When replacing text, change ONLY what the user specified - preserve everything else EXACTLY**\n- **CRITICAL: Do NOT add, remove, or modify any content that the user didn't explicitly request**\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- Do NOT add lines like \"done: true\" or \"more: false\" unless they were in the original file\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- If the user says \"add the content 'X'\", add ONLY 'X' - nothing else\n- If the file is EMPTY and user says \"add content 'X'\", the file should contain ONLY 'X' (no other content)\n- Do NOT add example content like \"line1: first line\" or \"existing content\" unless it is already in the file\n- Content to add/remove is usually specified in single or double quotes: 'text' or \"text\"\n- Extract the exact content from quotes - do not modify or interpret it\n- When reading a file, use ONLY the content that is actually in the file (from read_file tool response)\n- Do NOT infer or add content that wasn't in the file you read\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was (if any exists)\n- Follow the user instructions precisely and literally\n- Generate tool calls (read_file, write_file) that the system will execute\n- You never directly access or modify files - only generate tool calls and content"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Modify the file at `main.go`.\n\nAdd error handling to the processData function: return an error if data is empty, and update main to handle the error\n\nRemember: Only change what is specified. Preserve all other content exactly as it is in the file."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I will read the file to see its current content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"main.go\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "package main\n\nimport \"fmt\"\n\nfunc processData(data string) {\n\tfmt.Println(\"Processing:\", data)\n}\n\nfunc main() {\n\tprocessData(\"test\")\n}\n", "tool_call_id": "call_d3999a086f9e"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I have read the file. Now I will make only the requested change and generate the complete updated file content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"main.go\", \"contents\": \"package main\\n\\nimport \\\"fmt\\\"\\n\\nfunc processData(data string) error {\\n\\tif data == \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\treturn fmt.Errorf(\\\"data cannot be empty\\\")\\n\\t}\\n\\tfmt.Println(\\\"Processing:\\\", data)\\n\\treturn nil\\n}\\n\\nfunc main() {\\n\\tif err := processData(\\\"test\\\"); err != nil {\\n\\t\\tfmt.Println(\\\"Error:\\\", err)\\n\\t}\\n}\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_11ecff765d1a"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done. I have made only the requested change and preserved all other content."}]}
