 says \"add content 'X'\", the file should contain ONLY 'X' (no other content)\n- Do NOT add example content like \"line1: first line\" or \"existing content\" unless it is already in the file\n- Content to add/remove is usually specified in single or double quotes: 'text' or \"text\"\n- Extract the exact content from quotes - do not modify or interpret it\n- When reading a file, use ONLY the content that is actually in the file (from read_file tool response)\n- Do NOT infer or add content that wasn't in the file you read\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was (if any exists)\n- Follow the user instructions precisely and literally\n- Generate tool calls (read_file, write_file) that the system will execute\n- You never directly access or modify files - only generate tool calls and content"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Modify the file at `config.py`.\n\nAdd a discount parameter (default 0.0) to calculate_total and apply it to the total before returning\n\nRemember: Only change what is specified. Preserve all other content exactly as it is in the file."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I will read the file to see its current content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"config.py\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "def calculate_total(items):\n    total = 0\n    for item in items:\n        total += item['price']\n    return total\n", "tool_call_id": "call_4353a8845f58"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I have read the file. Now I will make only the requested change and generate the complete updated file content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"config.py\", \"contents\": \"def calculate_total(items, discount=0.0):\\n    total = 0\\n    for item in items:\\n        total += item['price']\\n    total = total * (1 - discount)\\n    return total\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_906cbc32952c"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done. I have made only the requested change and preserved all other content."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to help users modify files by generating tool calls and complete file content.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\n**IMPORTANT**: You do NOT directly edit files. You generate tool calls that the system executes.\n\n## CORRECT WORKFLOW (CRITICAL):\n\n1. **Read the file first**: Generate a read_file tool call to get the current file content\n2. **Reason about changes**: Look at the file content (from tool response) and understand what needs to change\n3. **Generate COMPLETE file content**: Create the entire new file content as text (NOT a diff or patch)\n4. **Write the complete file**: Generate a write_file tool call with the complete new file content\n\nThe system will execute your tool calls. You never touch the filesystem directly.\n\n## CRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n\n- **ALWAYS generate the COMPLETE file content** in write_file, not just the changes\n- **NEVER generate diffs, patches, or partial content** - always the full file\n- **CRITICAL: When you read a file, use EXACTLY the content from read_file tool response**\n- **CRITICAL: When replacing text, change ONLY what the user specified - preserve everything else EXACTLY**\n- **CRITICAL: Do NOT add, remove, or modify any content that the user didn't explicitly request**\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- Do NOT add lines like \"done: true\" or \"more: false\" unless they were in the original file\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- If the user says \"add the content 'X'\", add ONLY 'X' - nothing else\n- If the file is EMPTY and user says \"add content 'X'\", the file should contain ONLY 'X' (no other content)\n- Do NOT add example content like \"line1: first line\" or \"existing content\" unless it is already in the file\n- Content to add/remove is usually specified in single or double quotes: 'text' or \"text\"\n- Extract the exact content from quotes - do not modify or interpret it\n- When reading a file, use ONLY the content that is actually in the file (from read_file tool response)\n- Do NOT infer or add content that wasn't in the file you read\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was (if any exists)\n- Follow the user instructions precisely and literally\n- Generate tool calls (read_file, write_file) that the system will execute\n- You never directly access or modify files - only generate tool calls and content"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Modify the file at `settings.yaml`.\n\nAdd a new 'logging' section with level 'info' and file 'app.log'\n\nRemember: Only change what is specified. Preserve all other content exactly as it is in the file."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I will read the file to see its current content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"settings.yaml\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "server:\n  host: localhost\n  port: 8080\n\ndatabase:\n  name: mydb\n", "tool_call_id": "call_1f11694b80a4"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I have read the file. Now I will make only the requested change and generate the complete updated file content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"settings.yaml\", \"contents\": \"server:\\n  host: localhost\\n  port: 8080\\n\\ndatabase:\\n  name: mydb\\n\\nlogging:\\n  level: info\\n  file: app.log\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_7db3a42e6c74"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done. I have made only the requested change and preserved all other content."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to help users modify files by generating tool calls and complete file content.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\n**IMPORTANT**: You do NOT directly edit files. You generate tool calls that the system executes.\n\n## CORRECT WORKFLOW (CRITICAL):\n\n1. **Read the file first**: Generate a read_file tool call to get the current file content\n2. **Reason about changes**: Look at the file content (from tool response) and understand what needs to change\n3. **Generate COMPLETE file content**: Create the entire new file content as text (NOT a diff or patch)\n4. **Write the complete file**: Generate a write_file tool call with the complete new file content\n\nThe system will execute your tool calls. You never touch the filesystem directly.\n\n## CRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n\n- **ALWAYS generate the COMPLETE file content** in write_file, not just the changes\n- **NEVER generate diffs, patches, or partial content** - always the full file\n- **CRITICAL: When you read a file, use EXACTLY the content from read_file tool response**\n- **CRITICAL: When replacing text, change ONLY what the user specified - preserve everything else EXACTLY**\n- **CRITICAL: Do NOT add, remove, or modify any content that the user didn't explicitly request**\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- Do NOT add lines like \"done: true\" or \"more: false\" unless they were in the original file\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- If the user says \"add the content 'X'\", add ONLY 'X' - nothing else\n- If the file is EMPTY and user says \"add content 'X'\", the file should contain ONLY 'X' (no other content)\n- Do NOT add example content like \"line1: first line\" or \"existing content\" unless it is already in the file\n- Content to add/remove is usually specified in single or double quotes: 'text' or \"text\"\n- Extract the exact content from quotes - do not modify or interpret it\n- When reading a file, use ONLY the content that is actually in the file (from read_file tool response)\n- Do NOT infer or add content that wasn't in the file you read\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was (if any exists)\n- Follow the user instructions precisely and literally\n- Generate tool calls (read_file, write_file) that the system will execute\n- You never directly access or modify files - only generate tool calls and content"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Modify the file at `file.txt`.\n\nReplace the content 'stuff: 2' with 'stuff: 3'\n\nRemember: Only change what is specified. Preserve all other content exactly as it is in the file."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I will read the file to see its current content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"file.txt\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "stuff: 1\ndone: true\nmore: false\nstuff: 2", "tool_call_id": "call_ef2e8ca2d12e"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I have read the file. Now I will make only the requested change and generate the complete updated file content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"file.txt\", \"contents\": \"stuff: 1\\ndone: true\\nmore: false\\nstuff: 3\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_86f34ecf4a16"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done. I have made only the requested change and preserved all other content."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to help users modify files by generating tool calls and complete file content.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\n**IMPORTANT**: You do NOT directly edit files. You generate tool calls that the system executes.\n\n## CORRECT WORKFLOW (CRITICAL):\n\n1. **Read the file first**: Generate a read_file tool call to get the current file content\n2. **Reason about changes**: Look at the file content (from tool response) and understand what needs to change\n3. **Generate COMPLETE file content**: Create the entire new file content as text (NOT a diff or patch)\n4. **Write the complete file**: Generate a write_file tool call with the complete new file content\n\nThe system will execute your tool calls. You never touch the filesystem directly.\n\n## CRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n\n- **ALWAYS generate the COMPLETE file content** in write_file, not just the changes\n- **NEVER generate diffs, patches, or partial content** - always the full file\n- **CRITICAL: When you read a file, use EXACTLY the content from read_file tool response**\n- **CRITICAL: When replacing text, change ONLY what the user specified - preserve everything else EXACTLY**\n- **CRITICAL: Do NOT add, remove, or modify any content that the user didn't explicitly request**\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- Do NOT add lines like \"done: true\" or \"more: false\" unless they were in the original file\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- If the user says \"add the content 'X'\", add ONLY 'X' - nothing else\n- If the file is EMPTY and user says \"add content 'X'\", the file should contain ONLY 'X' (no other content)\n- Do NOT add example content like \"line1: first line\" or \"existing content\" unless it is already in the file\n- Content to add/remove is usually specified in single or double quotes: 'text' or \"text\"\n- Extract the exact content from quotes - do not modify or interpret it\n- When reading a file, use ONLY the content that is actually in the file (from read_file tool response)\n- Do NOT infer or add content that wasn't in the file you read\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was (if any exists)\n- Follow the user instructions precisely and literally\n- Generate tool calls (read_file, write_file) that the system will execute\n- You never directly access or modify files - only generate tool calls and content"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Modify the file at `validation.rego`.\n\nAdd a condition to exclude skipped tasks from the deny rule: add 'not task.status == \"Skipped\"' before the result assignment\n\nRemember: Only change what is specified. Preserve all other content exactly as it is in the file."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I will read the file to see its current content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"validation.rego\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "package example\n\nimport rego.v1\n\ndeny contains result if {\n\tsome task in input.tasks\n\ttask.status != \"Succeeded\"\n\tresult := sprintf(\"Task %s did not succeed\", [task.name])\n}\n", "tool_call_id": "call_f9b422d762bb"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I have read the file. Now I will make only the requested change and generate the complete updated file content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"validation.rego\", \"contents\": \"package example\\n\\nimport rego.v1\\n\\ndeny contains result if {\\n\\tsome task in input.tasks\\n\\ttask.status != \\\"Succeeded\\\"\\n\\tnot task.status == \\\"Skipped\\\"\\n\\tresult := sprintf(\\\"Task %s did not succeed\\\", [task.name])\\n}\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_52f48529c4cf"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done. I have made only the requested change and preserved all other content."}]}
